      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For WCAG 2.1 compliance focusing on color contrast ratios and screen reader compatibility, here's a quick checklist:\n\n1. **Color Contrast Ratios:**\n\t* Check that the minimum contrast ratio between background and foreground elements is 4.5 for normal text and 7 for large text.\n\t* Ensure that text is readable at 10pt - 14pt font size.\n2. **Screen Reader Compatibility:**\n\t* Verify that all interactive elements (e.g., buttons, links) have an ARIA attribute \"role\" and \"tabindex\" set to a positive integer.\n\t* Ensure that pages and elements can be navigated using only a keyboard.\n3. **Additional Tips:**\n\t* Use a color picker tool to calculate contrast ratios for different color combinations.\n\t* Test with popular screen readers like JAWS, NVDA, and VoiceOver.\n\nThis should give you a solid starting point for your accessibility audit.",
